1536
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,460
Lady Elianna.

1537
00:03:56,230 --> 00:03:58,430
How can we help you?

1538
00:03:58,430 --> 00:04:00,680
Help me?

1539
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:04,940
Yes. We were ordered to come here immediately
because you were in the archives.

1540
00:04:04,940 --> 00:04:05,960
Excuse me?

1541
00:04:05,960 --> 00:04:08,100
That's what Sara told us...

1542
00:04:11,870 --> 00:04:12,860
Shut your mouth.

1543
00:04:13,330 --> 00:04:14,410
But...

1544
00:04:14,410 --> 00:04:16,410
Someone's in there.

1545
00:04:16,410 --> 00:04:17,360
Call a guard.

1546
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,310
Wait.

1547
00:04:21,790 --> 00:04:24,600
Please stop this, Lady Matilda.

1548
00:04:24,600 --> 00:04:28,460
Just look for it already, Sara. You truly are dense.

1549
00:04:28,460 --> 00:04:34,710
The queen strictly controls
where Lady Eliannaâs dress is kept.

1550
00:04:36,490 --> 00:04:40,760
If she doesn't have a dress,
then look for something else that will be of use!

1551
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:41,970
Lady Matilda...

1552
00:04:42,420 --> 00:04:46,770
I need to steal her ideas and present them as my own
before she gets a chance.

1553
00:04:46,770 --> 00:04:49,230
I must stand out more than she does
at the Holy Night's Banquet,

1554
00:04:49,230 --> 00:04:52,950
or my grandfather and my mother will reprimand me!

1555
00:04:54,980 --> 00:05:02,490
Lady Sharon didn't have any useful information,
and since you're so useless, I have to struggle like this!

1556
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:05,240
But Lady Matilda, there is nothing more.

1557
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:08,870
It was us, the Dauner Family, who picked you up!

1558
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:18,130
Without our help, you couldn't support your family,
nor could you become a maid in the palace,

1559
00:05:18,660 --> 00:05:21,740
you filthy, cursed Azulan!

1560
00:05:22,890 --> 00:05:25,990
You know this, so repay your debt!

1561
00:05:31,190 --> 00:05:32,650
Lady Elianna...

1562
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:37,560
My, Lady Elianna.

1563
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:44,910
I heard that you had returned to your home,
but you have such a weak presence I didn't notice you here.

1564
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:50,910
To be neglecting your official duties this late in the game...
don't you feel any shame at all?

1565
00:05:50,910 --> 00:05:53,420
That was an aggressive shift in subject.

1566
00:05:53,420 --> 00:05:56,090
Your actions make others speak ill of the prince as well.

1567
00:05:56,090 --> 00:06:02,730
Those in the military say he is a
"weak-kneed prince who detests the art of war,"

1568
00:06:02,730 --> 00:06:06,180
and that our country will be in danger
should it be drawn into war in the future.

1569
00:06:06,450 --> 00:06:13,140
However, if I become a concubine,
those in the military will be much more at ease.

1570
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:15,440
We may be spending quite a bit of time together.

1571
00:06:29,940 --> 00:06:31,580
What is this?

1572
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:37,160
There's something called the Milulu clam
that can only be harvested in the tributary

1573
00:06:37,160 --> 00:06:39,590
where the Tessen and Mil Rivers meet in the Azul Region.

1574
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:48,220
I asked Sara to send for some.
It is processed to reproduce the ink of ancient manuscripts.

1575
00:06:48,660 --> 00:06:51,220
If that will be of use to you, take it.

1576
00:06:52,710 --> 00:06:57,940
Why would I want this bizarre, ancient ink...
And moreover, from the Azul Region?

1577
00:06:58,670 --> 00:07:02,320
Donât tell me you obtained this from Corba Village?

1578
00:07:02,760 --> 00:07:06,030
It is, but is something wrong with that?

1579
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:12,520
Do you understand what you are saying?
Corba Village... How nauseating.

1580
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,710
Lady Elianna!

1581
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:28,190
It seems you have some prejudice
against the Azul Region and Corba Village.

1582
00:07:28,190 --> 00:07:33,520
Is this because some say that the Ashen Nightmare
originated in the Azul Region?

1583
00:07:34,070 --> 00:07:35,940
Whatever else could it be?

1584
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:42,230
Sara is from Corba Village.
She is one of the loathsome and damned survivors.

1585
00:07:42,230 --> 00:07:44,480
You'll be infected if you get near her.

1586
00:07:45,530 --> 00:07:51,910
Those words could be taken as disrespectful towards the queen,
given how she battled and overcame the illness.

1587
00:07:54,020 --> 00:07:58,580
It's an unavoidable truth that I've invaded your room,

1588
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:02,800
however, do you have any idea
how your information got leaked?

1589
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:06,400
I see His Highness adores you,

1590
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:12,430
but whatever would you think if that information
was leaked by the one from the Azul Region?

1591
00:08:12,900 --> 00:08:17,480
They may also have to discontinue construction
of that bridge in progress.

1592
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:19,480
Lady Matilda.

1593
00:08:19,480 --> 00:08:21,690
It isn't Sara.

1594
00:08:22,690 --> 00:08:28,820
Both the queen and I are aware
that Sara is from the Corba Village.

1595
00:08:29,150 --> 00:08:33,200
If Sara were the one who spread information
about me to the Dauner family,

1596
00:08:33,460 --> 00:08:39,370
then Lady Matilda would have known
that I had Sara help me obtain the Milulu clams.

1597
00:08:39,370 --> 00:08:41,080
W-Well...

1598
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:46,710
And, about Corba Village,
there's something you're misunderstanding.

1599
00:08:46,710 --> 00:08:47,970
Huh?

1600
00:08:49,290 --> 00:08:51,390
Around mid-winter some fifteen years ago,

1601
00:08:51,390 --> 00:08:54,970
before the "Ashen Nightmare"
came to be known by that name,

1602
00:08:55,710 --> 00:08:59,190
the Tessen River flooded
due to unprecedented torrential rains,

1603
00:08:59,190 --> 00:09:02,790
and many of the bridges spanning the river
were washed away.

1604
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:08,070
The Azul Region, which relied on the bridges
to commune with other territories,

1605
00:09:08,070 --> 00:09:10,780
became like a solitary island on the continent.

1606
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:18,000
Under those circumstances, the plague spread through the country
from the northeastern area, including Azul.

1607
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:21,230
Corba was an especially impoverished village.

1608
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:26,780
After getting the autumn harvest from the mountains,
the men had to live away from home to work.

1609
00:09:27,810 --> 00:09:34,470
The people left in the village
had to fight off the plague, alone and unaided.

1610
00:09:35,730 --> 00:09:39,390
It was only by the end of winter
that help arrived at the village.

1611
00:09:39,390 --> 00:09:42,270
It was suspected that there were no survivors.

1612
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:48,630
However, the people of the village supported each other,
and losses were kept to a minimum.

1613
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:52,780
At first, it was called a miracle.

1614
00:09:53,380 --> 00:09:56,600
But, though those were the only losses they had,

1615
00:09:56,600 --> 00:10:02,500
voices of doubt started to rise
about why Corba Village was still surviving.

1616
00:10:03,500 --> 00:10:07,920
"Perhaps the Ashen Nightmare originated in Corba Village."

1617
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:09,840
Is that wrong?

1618
00:10:09,840 --> 00:10:12,420
It was a baseless rumor.

1619
00:10:12,980 --> 00:10:17,930
People may have wanted a scapegoat for their hatred.

1620
00:10:17,930 --> 00:10:23,690
None of them had any regard for how
those on the receiving end of this animosity felt.

1621
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:27,310
The plague <i>did</i> actually originate in the Azul Region, though,

1622
00:10:27,310 --> 00:10:30,570
and there's no proof that the survivors
of the Corba Village are not cursed.

1623
00:10:34,180 --> 00:10:38,950
The Ashen Nightmare did not originate in the Corba Village.

1624
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:45,460
According to research, some medical scholars
believe that the disease resembles the plague

1625
00:10:45,460 --> 00:10:48,840
that was one of the causes
of the destruction of the Kai Arg Empire.

1626
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:51,210
B-But Corba Village isâ

1627
00:10:51,570 --> 00:10:54,550
The only way in and out of the village was by a bridge,

1628
00:10:54,550 --> 00:10:57,930
and the men were not present
due to working outside of the village to make a living,

1629
00:10:57,930 --> 00:11:00,150
and that is the cause of this tragedy.

1630
00:11:01,710 --> 00:11:04,980
Sauslind and the regional lord's neglect
were responsible for this.

1631
00:11:06,060 --> 00:11:08,230
The people of the village are victims.

1632
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:13,330
Are you speaking seriously right now?
How could you blame the state?

1633
00:11:13,330 --> 00:11:16,610
It would be a serious matter
if you made a statement like that!

1634
00:11:16,610 --> 00:11:21,420
His Highness dealing with the bridge
in the Azul Region right now,

1635
00:11:21,420 --> 00:11:28,580
is manifestation of the determination
that the same tragedy must not and will not happen again.

1636
00:11:28,580 --> 00:11:34,760
The policies put forth for the dignity of my country
will not be reversed by me alone.

1637
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:37,320
The people are the treasure of their country.

1638
00:11:37,320 --> 00:11:40,260
Without its citizens, neither king nor country will exist.

1639
00:11:40,550 --> 00:11:44,560
I would never accept anyone
as a potential concubine for His Highness

1640
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:48,770
who cannot grasp such simple things,
and despises the people she's committed to protect!

1641
00:11:48,770 --> 00:11:49,770
What?!

1642
00:11:52,400 --> 00:11:54,530
How dare you speak to me as if I were a child!

1643
00:11:54,530 --> 00:11:55,530
Please, stop!

1644
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:58,280
Sara!

1645
00:11:58,650 --> 00:11:59,960
Let it go!

1646
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:01,280
Lady Matilâ

1647
00:12:03,410 --> 00:12:05,200
How awful!

1648
00:12:05,520 --> 00:12:07,360
What have you done?!

1649
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,960
Excuse me.

1650
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:19,720
I tried to say something earlier,
but I doubt you heard me over the commotion.

1651
00:12:19,720 --> 00:12:20,590
Your Hiâ

1652
00:12:20,590 --> 00:12:21,850
Prince Christopher!

1653
00:12:22,930 --> 00:12:26,100
Lady Elianna used that maid to ruin my dress...

1654
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,560
Eek! Wh-What are you doing?!

1655
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:32,700
Let's see... caught in the midst
of attempted assault on the lady.

1656
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:33,490
What?!

1657
00:12:33,490 --> 00:12:36,110
Also, perpetrating falsehoods against the crown prince,

1658
00:12:36,110 --> 00:12:40,360
and the crime of contempt against
the fiancÃ©e of the crown prince... that sounds about right.

1659
00:12:40,670 --> 00:12:42,370
Let me go, you insolent brute!

1660
00:12:42,370 --> 00:12:46,000
Once I report this to my grandfather,
you are entirely done for!

1661
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:50,000
Huh... I might actually take that over serving the demon lord.

1662
00:12:50,390 --> 00:12:51,500
Jean.

1663
00:12:52,220 --> 00:12:55,290
Let go! Your Highness, this personâ

1664
00:12:55,290 --> 00:12:56,510
Good grief.

1665
00:12:56,510 --> 00:13:04,510
This keeps happening, over and over.
Do people genuinely think I canât discern a truth from a lie?

1666
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:10,520
Lady Matilda Dauner...

1667
00:13:10,520 --> 00:13:14,770
Your grandfather is admittedly
an important figure in the military,

1668
00:13:14,770 --> 00:13:18,150
but he should act with more caution
when dealing with young people like me.

1669
00:13:19,330 --> 00:13:24,660
However, I'm thinking the time has come for him
to resign and make way for the next generation.

1670
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:29,460
The Dorud Company which the Dauner family has capital in
is in competition with the Mers Company,

1671
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:32,170
which the royal family makes use of.

1672
00:13:32,170 --> 00:13:37,250
I've heard itâs common among merchants
to send one of their subordinates in to infiltrate the opposition,

1673
00:13:37,250 --> 00:13:40,050
but they picked the wrong people to mess with.

1674
00:13:40,050 --> 00:13:46,470
The Dorud company has scandalous rumors floating
around about it, and I could have taken then down, but...

1675
00:13:46,470 --> 00:13:49,520
I decided to replace the head and engage with them.

1676
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:54,270
The new chairman should soon cut off
support to the Dauner family.

1677
00:13:54,270 --> 00:13:55,560
You can't...

1678
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:59,820
The Dorud Company was shouldering
all the debt your house owes, as well...

1679
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:03,780
Well, it's obvious where the Dauner family is headed.

1680
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:12,500
Now, about all the talk about harems and such, the Dauner family
are the only ones who spouted that kind of nonsense.

1681
00:14:12,500 --> 00:14:15,830
No other nobles have said anything of the sort.

1682
00:14:17,090 --> 00:14:20,710
Elianna will be my <i>only</i> consort.

1683
00:14:22,040 --> 00:14:26,220
There will be no other women beside me. None.

1684
00:14:27,620 --> 00:14:28,710
Take her away.

1685
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:35,430
Sara, you will be dealt with shortly. You may go.

1686
00:14:46,740 --> 00:14:47,490
Eli...

1687
00:14:53,650 --> 00:14:55,270
<i>I have to apologize.</i>

1688
00:14:56,230 --> 00:14:58,630
<i>I have to apologize to His Highness...</i>

1689
00:14:59,570 --> 00:15:05,530
<i>His Highness must be disappointed in my cowardly escape.</i>

1690
00:15:08,130 --> 00:15:09,900
I'm sorry, Eli.

1691
00:15:11,330 --> 00:15:14,390
This is my fault. I'm sorry.

1692
00:15:15,150 --> 00:15:18,430
<i>Why is His Highness apologizing?</i>

1693
00:15:19,610 --> 00:15:25,650
<i>I'm the one who worried on my own
then came to my own conclusions.</i>

1694
00:15:25,650 --> 00:15:29,100
<i>My heart became so full of jealousy...</i>

1695
00:15:30,210 --> 00:15:35,040
<i>Even now, I've hurt the person I love.</i>

1696
00:15:37,350 --> 00:15:39,040
Your Highness...

1697
00:15:41,380 --> 00:15:48,050
Your Highness, you've done... nothing wrong. I was...

1698
00:15:55,680 --> 00:15:56,550
I'm sorry.

1699
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:01,500
Eli, I'm sorry.

1700
00:16:04,240 --> 00:16:11,070
<i>After that, I talked about the anxieties
that burdened my heart one by one...</i>

1701
00:16:11,810 --> 00:16:15,040
<i>Not being able to become like Queen Henrietta...</i>

1702
00:16:15,040 --> 00:16:20,080
<i>The misappropriation of my remarks
that happened despite trying to do my best... </i><i></i>

1703
00:16:21,300 --> 00:16:27,130
<i>Realizing once again how terrifying the palace could be
and being discouraged by it. </i><i></i>

1704
00:16:27,130 --> 00:16:32,010
<i>The anxiety I had about the proposals
for His Highness' to have concubines... </i><i></i>

1705
00:16:32,010 --> 00:16:36,870
<i>The doubt that gnawed at me
on seeing the connection between him and Lady Mireille... </i><i></i>

1706
00:16:40,640 --> 00:16:45,110
I knew I had to ask you, Your Highness,
but I was so afraid...

1707
00:16:45,110 --> 00:16:48,240
and moreover, I couldn't become a burden to you.

1708
00:16:49,070 --> 00:16:57,980
I thought my failures held you back,
and it was so painful and miserable...

1709
00:16:58,880 --> 00:17:04,250
Eli, that isn't the slightest bit true.
You haven't done anything wrong.

1710
00:17:04,710 --> 00:17:06,870
Your Highness, it isn't your fault.

1711
00:17:10,170 --> 00:17:14,230
I know that you are very earnest
and always try too hard, and yet...

1712
00:17:14,230 --> 00:17:20,270
I should have considered that
and stayed by your side. I'm sorry.

1713
00:17:23,660 --> 00:17:27,310
The thing with Lady Lamond
is truly just a misunderstanding.

1714
00:17:28,340 --> 00:17:33,470
I know that you've been devoting yourself
to official business you aren't yet used to,

1715
00:17:33,470 --> 00:17:36,140
so I was going to take care of it on my end.

1716
00:17:37,950 --> 00:17:40,140
You're seeing my bad habit now, huh?

1717
00:17:41,490 --> 00:17:45,000
My mistake was trying to resolve everything on my own.

1718
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,300
Your Highness...

1719
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:52,550
Still, thatâs the first time
Iâve ever seen you cry out of concern for me, Eli.

1720
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:56,050
I almost want to see it happen again...

1721
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:05,690
What do you mean
there was a commotion in Elianna's room?

1722
00:18:05,690 --> 00:18:06,440
Crap...

1723
00:18:06,850 --> 00:18:08,950
What did Chris do?

1724
00:18:16,210 --> 00:18:18,700
They've run away, those children.

1725
00:18:18,700 --> 00:18:24,710
According to a maid, Earl Dauner's granddaughter
entered the room without permission.

1726
00:18:25,190 --> 00:18:30,350
The Dauner family just never learns, do they? But...

1727
00:18:30,350 --> 00:18:33,750
It looks like Chris has finally run out of patience.

1728
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:39,770
He would not dislike her
for such a small thing of that magnitude.

1729
00:18:39,770 --> 00:18:40,930
Besides,

1730
00:18:41,280 --> 00:18:47,770
though the Holy Night's Banquet is the day after tomorrow,
Elianna's jewelry has yet to be decided.

1731
00:18:47,770 --> 00:18:51,820
Still, he monopolizes Elianna <i>every</i> single time...

1732
00:18:51,820 --> 00:18:55,950
and I've refrained from inviting her frequently
to social gatherings because

1733
00:18:55,950 --> 00:18:58,950
he told me she'd run away
if I kept interrupting her reading time.

1734
00:18:59,860 --> 00:19:04,080
Now sheâs about to slip out of our grasp
because of my own sonâs incompetence?

1735
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:06,210
Goodness... How shameful.

1736
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:09,730
My Queen, it's time for your next appointment.

1737
00:19:17,970 --> 00:19:22,540
What's so bad about keeping your fiancÃ©e to yourself?

1738
00:19:24,110 --> 00:19:31,020
Eli, I think you may not have noticed,
but my mother started liking you four years ago.

1739
00:19:31,020 --> 00:19:31,730
Huh?

1740
00:19:36,770 --> 00:19:43,200
My mother repeatedly invited you to tea parties
when you had just become my fianceÃ©, right?

1741
00:19:43,200 --> 00:19:47,870
That was because she wanted so desperately
to show everyone her new daughter-in-law.

1742
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:52,090
You wouldn't be able to resist fawning
over getting all close and personal

1743
00:19:52,090 --> 00:19:55,010
with someone you respect and strive to be like, would you?

1744
00:19:56,050 --> 00:20:01,260
The reason sheâs being so tough on you is because
youâre downright adorable, and she canât help it.

1745
00:20:01,930 --> 00:20:04,770
Sheâs just not very upfront about her feelings.

1746
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:08,710
There's absolutely nothing wrong
with you the way you are.

1747
00:20:10,050 --> 00:20:15,530
It's important to strive for perfection,
but don't get caught up in only doing that.

1748
00:20:18,390 --> 00:20:22,370
You, who thinks about the people first and foremost,
are fine the way you are,

1749
00:20:22,370 --> 00:20:26,870
and as someone who stands by my side, you are worthy.

1750
00:20:26,870 --> 00:20:28,040
Your Highness...

1751
00:20:28,340 --> 00:20:34,670
At your back, Eli, are the people of Sauslind
who you are trying to protect with all your might.

1752
00:20:35,500 --> 00:20:41,300
Everyone knows that, so there's no ground
for my so-called "concubines" to stand on.

1753
00:20:42,050 --> 00:20:49,000
Your presence alone protects and supports me,
so if you ever lose confidence in yourself...

1754
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,530
Iâll be more than happy to remind you of that.

1755
00:20:53,400 --> 00:21:01,410
<i>The reality of becoming a princess
unknowingly made me feel overwhelmed and terrified me,</i>

1756
00:21:01,410 --> 00:21:09,310
<i>but to me, I am fine as I am now,
and there is a beloved person by my side who says so.</i>

1757
00:21:10,350 --> 00:21:14,090
Is there anything else you want to ask me, Eli?

1758
00:21:16,700 --> 00:21:18,340
I...

1759
00:21:21,220 --> 00:21:25,010
Please don't marry another woman besides me.

1760
00:21:28,980 --> 00:21:31,910
Eli, that's breaking the rules.

1761
00:21:31,910 --> 00:21:33,520
Your Highness...

1762
00:21:33,520 --> 00:21:36,460
I don't need anyone but you, Eli.

1763
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:42,240
Even if you run, I'll catch you every time.

1764
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:49,920
If it were that easy to give up on my emotions,
I wouldn't be in such pain.

1765
00:21:52,590 --> 00:21:58,460
Eli, don't ever doubt my feelings.

1766
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:06,960
I love you, Christopher... I will never run away again.

